# Trivy suppressions (owner decision #629, option 1, 2026-10-26).
# Every entry MUST carry an `exp:` date: Trivy reports the finding again
# once it passes, so a suppression can never become permanent by accident.
# Only dev / build-time tooling may be listed here, never shipped code.
# Exception: shipped-code entries only by an explicit owner decision, short
# expiry, with the fix tracked in an open issue (see decode-uri-component, #776).

# body-parser 2.3.0 (frontend/package-lock.json), DoS via an unhandled
# decompression stream error. Pulled in by @react-native-community/cli-server-api
# (the Metro dev server), not shipped in the app or backend. The fix (2.4.0,
# in range) was published 2026-10-22; bump it with `npm update body-parser`
# once it is two weeks old (2026-11-05) and delete this entry.
CVE-2026-111181 exp:2026-11-06

# zod 3.25.76 under expo/node_modules (@expo/cli, Expo SDK 56), DoS via
# unbounded array validation. Build-time CLI only. Fixed only in zod 4.6.6,
# which @expo/cli ^3.25.76 does not accept; fix with the next Expo SDK
# upgrade. Expires after 90 days so it is reviewed again.
CVE-2023-54404 exp:2027-01-24

# decode-uri-component 0.2.2 (frontend/package-lock.json, via query-string@7 /
# React Navigation), DoS via quadratic replacement of percent-encoded runs.
# SHIPPED app code (deep-link / URL parsing). Owner decision on #776
# (2026-10-30): suppress for now, keep #776 open for the real fix (npm
# override to >=0.5.1 or a navigation upgrade with SDK 58, #712). Short expiry
# on purpose: if #776 isn't fixed by then, Trivy fails again.
CVE-2026-118664 exp:2026-11-29
